{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Will you indeed reign over us, or will you indeed rule over us?</b> Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 37:8) explained: Shall we set you up as king over us, or will you rule over us by force? But more correct is the opinion of Onkelos (Targum Onkelos on Genesis 37:8): Will you be king over us, or a ruler ruling over us — for to both of them a man bows down — meaning, you will never be over us, neither as king nor as ruler. And the sense of \"for his dreams and for his words\" is that they hated him on account of the dreams and also on account of the telling, that he would recount it to them as one boasting, as he said, \"Hear, please, this dream which I have dreamed.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:51.192107669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}